{"content":[{"c":["BAALATH-BEER"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Place-name meaning “mistress” or “lady of the well.” Like the masculine counterpart Baal, Baalath often appears in a compound place-name. It seems to suggest that the Canaanite goddess Baalath, patron of Byblos, was associated with the particular place or well. Baalath-beer was the name of a town in Simeon’s tribe, also identified as Baal or Baalath (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.4.33","r":"1Chr.4.33","rawR":"1Chr.4.33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.4.33","value":"1Chr.4.33"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 4:33"},"), Ramah of the Negev (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.19.8","r":"Josh.19.8","rawR":"Josh.19.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.19.8","value":"Josh.19.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 19:8"},"), and Ramoth of the Negev (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.30.27","r":"1Sam.30.27","rawR":"1Sam.30.27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.30.27","value":"1Sam.30.27"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 30:27"},"). It may have marked the southern limits of Simeon’s inheritance."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"BaalathBeer","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"1 Chr 4:33","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.4.33","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.4.33","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.4.33"},{"anchorText":"Jos 19:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.19.8","rawQueryValue":"Josh.19.8","sourceRefExact":"Josh.19.8"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 30:27","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.30.27","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.30.27","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.30.27"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"3540908600a47bd6adc4c2be4d2583a6c2e6c0c80de3d851fe032499d3f9711a","sourceItemName":"BaalathBeer","sourceItemOrder":6,"sourceMember":"Articles/B.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"BaalathBeer","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Baalath-Beer","title":"Baalath-Beer","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}